---

## Overview

This project implements a multi-branch enterprise WAN in GNS3, connecting
Headquarters to five branch offices — Lahore, Karachi, Islamabad, Peshawar,
and Multan — using secure point-to-point WAN links, dynamic routing, and a
redundant backup path. The goal is to demonstrate that every branch retains
connectivity to Headquarters even if its primary WAN link fails, with no
manual intervention required.

---

## Topology

- **15** Cisco c3745 routers
- **6** Ethernet switches
- **6** client PCs (VPCS)

**Router groups:**

| Group | Routers | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Primary (EDGE1) | HQ-EDGE1, LHR-EDGE1, KHI-EDGE1, ISB-EDGE1, PEW-EDGE1, MUL-EDGE1 | Chain topology carrying primary WAN traffic; each also serves the site LAN (switch + 2 PCs) |
| Backup (EDGE2) | HQ-EDGE2, LHR-EDGE2, KHI-EDGE2, ISB-EDGE2, PEW-EDGE2, MUL-EDGE2 | Connected internally to their site's EDGE1 and externally to the core mesh; no LAN traffic |
| Core transit | CORE-T1, CORE-T2, CORE-T3 | Backbone ring carrying the backup path between branch EDGE2 routers and HQ-EDGE2 |

**Primary chain:** `HQ → LHR → KHI → ISB → PEW → MUL`
**Backup mesh:** `Branch EDGE2 → CORE-T1 / T2 / T3 (ring) → HQ-EDGE2` (via GRE tunnels)

---

## Technologies Implemented

| Technology | Details |
|---|---|
| **PPP + CHAP** | Enabled on every WAN-facing serial link; each router authenticates its neighbor by hostname/password before the link passes traffic |
| **OSPF** | Single-area (Area 0) process on all 15 routers, using one wildcard network statement |
| **GRE Tunnels** | Logical tunnels between HQ-EDGE2 and every branch EDGE2, sourced from loopback addresses so they stay stable regardless of the underlying physical path |
| **Floating Static Routes** | Default route (AD 150) on each branch EDGE1 pointing to its local EDGE2, activating automatically if the primary OSPF route is withdrawn |
| **NAT/PAT** | Overload (PAT) configured on HQ-EDGE1 for LAN-to-WAN address translation |

